r next call using that `Git` instance (`r.repo.git`) only. No need to reset.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487232601,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MDI2MTQ4MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1284#issuecomment-280261481"},"message":"Not sure, whether we want to integrate this in the `GitRepo` methods, since it's a one-liner anyway.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487232635,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MDI2MTYwOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1284#issuecomment-280261609"},"message":"thanks, will try that.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487232863,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MDI2MjQ0Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1284#issuecomment-280262442"},"message":"Thinking of integration - there's a reason to do it indeed. That is: How to pass options to git ATM depends on the `GitRepo` method, since it's different if don't use GitPython therein. So it would be nice to have consistent way for the Repo classes. Therefore keep that issue open, but may be it's not as urgent as assumed before.","files":null}]}